{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1489447-princesses-and-beasts-because-they-can-get-along","id":1489447,"title":"Princesses and Beasts - Because they CAN Get Along","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-07T19:15:16-07:00","id":1489447,"title":"Princesses and Beasts - Because they CAN Get Along","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">There was a thread about possible friendships between these two specific groups a while back, but it\u2019s long dead and so I thought I might start a new one. The problem I\u2019ve always found with the idea that the two groups can <i>never</i> get along is that it assumes homogeny within both Nobles and Beasts, that none of them will like each other due to their opposing themes. And while sure, it makes sense that many wouldn\u2019t get along, that falls apart when you consider that Nobles and Beasts are still, for lack of a better word, people, and will naturally find things to bond over and work together for. And I\u2019m not just talking about Beasts and the Twilight Courts. It only takes a little imagination to come up with ways for Radiant Court Nobles to work with Beasts.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Here are some examples I came up with pretty quickly:</span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">- A Seeker of Spades and an Ugallu Whisper, teaming up to uncover and expose the secrets of corrupt politicians and rich assholes. </span></span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">- A Clubs Noble who adores bugs, finding beauty in a Namtaru who\u2019s always been reviled. </span></span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">- Two siblings, one who experiences a Devouring, the other a Blossoming, who insist on staying together in this new world no matter what. </span></span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">- An Eshmaki Nemesis and Champion of Swords, hunting evil from both the shadows and the light, so there is nowhere to hide. </span></span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">- A Noble hunting down a rampaging Ruin Horror, finding out that the reason the Horror was so hungry was because its Beast had just experienced her devouring and hated the idea of ruining others lives to feed her hunger. The two trying to come up with a solution that will satisfy the Horror without hurting innocents, while also dealing with arriving Heroes, who care much less than the Beast does about collateral. </span></span></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If anyone else has any potential story ideas, possible nightmares, etc. feel free to share! I\u2019d love to hear them. I just think it\u2019s important to remember that not all Beasts and Nobles are stereotypes, and in the right circumstances, they could make a rather terrifying team.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27217-skyewards","name":"Skyewards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T04:21:15-07:00","id":1489543,"title":"","content":"Admittedly, I've always liked the idea of a Noble and a Beast eventually getting together in a romantic relationship, so there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-09T15:30:57-07:00","id":1489586,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s a couple of things to add onto my earlier post;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skyewards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1489447-princesses-and-beasts-because-they-can-get-along#post1489447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">- Two siblings, one who experiences a Devouring, the other a Blossoming, who insist on staying together in this new world no matter what. </span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>This could be an interesting starting point for creating a combination Brood-Nakama/Clique, if each sibling were to reach out into their respective supernatural communities\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skyewards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1489447-princesses-and-beasts-because-they-can-get-along#post1489447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If anyone else has any potential story ideas, possible nightmares, etc. feel free to share! I\u2019d love to hear them. I just think it\u2019s important to remember that not all Beasts and Nobles are stereotypes, and in the right circumstances, they could make a rather terrifying team.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree on the point of them potentially being completely terrifying when they\u2019re cooperating in/under the right circumstances. I haven\u2019t got any story hook ideas, or nightmares, but I\u2019ve been thinking of trying to develop some proper stereotypes that the different Callings and Courts of the Enlightened, and the various Families and Hungers of the Begotten could have on each other.<br /> <br /> Actually, I think I once proposed an antagonist concept or two for this crossover\u2026 Yeah, I did! Only one I can remember off the toppa\u2019 my head is that of an Insatiable who\u2019d <i>somehow</i> gotten the backing of the Darkness, be it due to the making of some sort of deal or pact, the latter somehow managing to partially corrupt the former(?), or something else entirely.<br /> <br /> Basically the idea I had at the time was that of an enemy that only the combined knowledge, understanding, powers, and skills, of both splats could ensure victory. And that the scenario occurred in the early days of the Light\u2019s proper return to earth, when it\u2019s scions had just started learning about the spawn of the Dark Mother, in a location where tensions where particularly high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 08-09-2022, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T21:42:25-07:00","id":1492951,"title":"","content":"Saw this and got me thinking, sadly I don't know much about princess, but I know a bit about Beast, so I cooked a quick nightmare idea, basically weaponizing a protective instinct, got the idea of aiming a mama bear at someone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Someone is threathening them</b><br /> <i>They aren't safe, I got to protect them</i><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Satiety Vs Composure + Supernatural Resistance<br /> <b>Normal:</b> The target is aflicted with the obsession condition in regard to protecting something or someone they hold dear, to the exclusion of everything else, convinced that they are at risk, real or not.<br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The target becomes immune to the Beaten down tilt, the only way they'll stop is through full incapacitation, unconciousness or death.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> For every point of satiety spent the target of this nightmare benefits from rote action for rolls that are in line with their obsession.<br /> <br /> Like I said above, just a quickly cooked nightmare, I'm aiming mostly at the themes of Princess since they are magical girls and thinking more of the Heroic ones, it's a bit hard to come up with fears that involve a heroic drive, but I tend to get the idea that it involves a lot about the necessary lengths that the heroic characters need to go to or the price of failure if they falter, quoting certain salarian scientist &quot;had to be me someone else might've gotten it wrong&quot; can be driven by a fear of the heroic goal not being achieved.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just my two cents.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T22:51:17-07:00","id":1492955,"title":"","content":"Oooo, that does look interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27217-skyewards","name":"Skyewards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T15:20:57-07:00","id":1493029,"title":"","content":"I though aobut things a bit more, and I really don't see any point on the argument that Beast and Princesses must be enemies, yeah beast do have to be violent against others to feed be it psychologically or physically, but what about acceptable targets of such violence? Dark Eras Companion (Pg. 234) put a particular good setting for this kind of thing, during the Civil War in the USA and its aftermath, Beast were in both sides of the conflict, so let's put a spin on a more moral and altruistic Beast using that as a base.<br /> <br /> A collector that steals away slaves from their owners, he doesn't take one or two, but the whole plantation to make sure the owners feel the loss.<br /> A Ravager that burns down the holdings of slave traffickers.<br /> A Tyrant taking control of the goverment and thwarting the actions of corrupt officials by taking the power to himself (Really this could be in any setting, unless you make it a corruption free utopia)<br /> Any Nemesis that considers slavery as something bad.<br /> <br /> What about another mainstream example? with Bruce Banner and the Hulk, not the Professor Hulk but before that, Avengers age of Ultron shows us an out of control Hulk, but the Hulk is part of the Heroes team in part precisely because of that destructive potential, just aimed at an acceptable target, also consider that first Avenger movie and what happened with Loki, did you object to his violent treatment at the hands of the Hulk?<br /> <br /> Really that whole argument ignores that even without supernatural influence vanilla mortal Humans can be absolubtly awful against each other, can you think of anyone deserving the Begotten package deal of trauma? then you have the potential to make a compelling story with both Beast and Princess as they both use their unique perpesctives to deliver Karmic justice to someone.<br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry if this comes out a bit like a rant.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","user":"Aeveth","date":". 09-17-2022, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}